#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:4
msgid "FIR filter design"
msgstr "Projeto de filtros FIR"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:7
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr "Motivação"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:9
msgid ""
"In the chaotic communication scheme, a finite impulse response (FIR) "
"filter is inserted **inside the Hénon feedback loop**.  This turns the "
"standard 2‑D map into a higher‑dimensional system whose dynamics are "
"shaped by the filter coefficients."
msgstr ""
"No esquema de comunicação caótica, um filtro de resposta ao impulso "
"finita (FIR) é inserido **dentro do laço de realimentação de Hénon**.  "
"Isso transforma o mapa 2‑D padrão em um sistema de dimensão mais alta "
"cuja dinâmica é moldada pelos coeficientes do filtro."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:14
msgid "The motivation is two‑fold:"
msgstr "A motivação é dupla:"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:16
msgid ""
"**Band‑limiting.**  Chaotic signals produced by the unfiltered Hénon map "
"have a broad, flat spectrum.  Real communication channels have limited "
"bandwidth ; the FIR filter constrains the chaotic signal to occupy only "
"the desired frequency band."
msgstr ""
"**Limitação de banda.**  Sinais caóticos produzidos pelo mapa de Hénon "
"não filtrado têm um espectro amplo e plano.  Canais de comunicação reais "
"têm largura de banda limitada: o filtro FIR restringe o sinal caótico a "
"ocupar apenas a faixa de frequência desejada."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Controllable chaos.**  By varying the filter order and cutoff, we can "
"study which filter parameters *preserve* chaos and which *suppress* it : "
"the core empirical question of the PFC."
msgstr ""
"**Caos controlável.**  Variando a ordem e a frequência de corte do "
"filtro, podemos estudar quais parâmetros *preservam* o caos e quais o "
"*suprimem*: a questão empírica central do PFC."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:26
msgid "``firwin`` vs. MATLAB ``fir1``"
msgstr "``firwin`` vs. MATLAB ``fir1``"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:28
msgid ""
"The project uses :func:`scipy.signal.firwin` rather than implementing its"
" own FIR design.  There is a documented off‑by‑one difference relative to"
" MATLAB's ``fir1``:"
msgstr ""
"O projeto usa :func:`scipy.signal.firwin` em vez de implementar seu "
"próprio projeto FIR.  Há uma diferença off‑by‑one documentada em relação "
"ao ``fir1`` do MATLAB:"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:32
msgid "MATLAB: ``fir1(N, wc)`` produces ``N+1`` coefficients."
msgstr "MATLAB: ``fir1(N, wc)`` produz ``N+1`` coeficientes."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:33
msgid "SciPy: ``firwin(N, wc)`` produces ``N`` coefficients."
msgstr "SciPy: ``firwin(N, wc)`` produz ``N`` coeficientes."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:35
msgid ""
"To obtain the same filter as MATLAB's ``fir1(N, wc)``, call ``firwin(N+1,"
" wc)``.  The ``chaotic-pfc`` codebase consistently uses ``firwin(Nss, "
"wc)`` where ``Nss`` is the number of filter taps (coefficients), which "
"matches the convention used in the academic article."
msgstr ""
"Para obter o mesmo filtro do ``fir1(N, wc)`` do MATLAB, chame "
"``firwin(N+1, wc)``.  O código do ``chaotic-pfc`` consistentemente usa "
"``firwin(Nss, wc)`` onde ``Nss`` é o número de coeficientes do filtro, "
"que corresponde à convenção usada no artigo acadêmico."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:41
msgid ""
"The ``fs=2`` default in ``firwin`` means ``wc`` is in units of "
":math:`\\pi` rad/sample — consistent with the normalisation "
":math:`\\omega_c / \\pi` used throughout the sweep literature."
msgstr ""
"The ``fs=2`` default in ``firwin`` means ``wc`` is in units of "
":math:`\\\\pi` rad/sample — consistent with the normalisation "
":math:`\\omega_c / \\\\pi` used throughout the sweep literature."

