"A coluna **atenuação na banda de rejeição** é a atenuação entregue pelo "
"filtro projetado; a coluna **pico de lóbulo lateral** é o nível da "
"própria janela, conforme a Tabela I do artigo (adaptada de "
"[Harris1978]_)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:132
msgid ""
"**Kaiser window** deserves special attention.  The shape parameter "
":math:`\\beta` controls the trade‑off between main‑lobe width and "
"sidelobe level.  The project includes a dedicated :math:`\\beta`-sweep "
"(``chaotic-pfc run sweep beta-sweep``) that evaluates Lyapunov exponents "
"across :math:`\\beta \\in [2, 14]` in steps of :math:`0.5` for each "
"filter type."
msgstr ""
"**Kaiser window** deserves special attention.  The shape parameter "
":math:`\\beta` controls the trade‑off between main‑lobe width and "
"sidelobe level.  The project includes a dedicated :math:`\\beta`-sweep "
"(``chaotic-pfc run sweep beta-sweep``) that evaluates Lyapunov exponents "
"across :math:`\\beta \\in [2, 14]` in steps of :math:`0.5` for each "
"filter type."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:140
msgid "Stability and the fixed point"
msgstr "Estabilidade e o ponto fixo"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:142
msgid ""
"When an FIR filter is inserted into the Hénon feedback loop, the Jacobian"
" matrix grows from :math:`2 \\times 2` to :math:`K \\times K`, where "
":math:`K = N_s` for :math:`N_s \\ge 3` (and :math:`K = 2` for :math:`N_s "
"\\le 2`), with :math:`N_s` the number of filter coefficients that feed "
"back into the dynamics.  The implementation reserves one extra auxiliary "
"state slot for :math:`N_s = 3`."
msgstr ""
"Quando um filtro FIR é inserido no laço de realimentação de Hénon, a "
"matriz Jacobiana cresce de :math:`2 \\times 2` para :math:`K \\times K`, "
"onde :math:`K = N_s` para :math:`N_s \\ge 3` (e :math:`K = 2` para "
":math:`N_s \\le 2`), sendo :math:`N_s` o número de coeficientes do filtro"
" que realimentam a dinâmica.  A implementação reserva um espaço auxiliar "
"extra no estado para :math:`N_s = 3`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:149
msgid ""
"The **fixed point** of the combined map‑plus‑filter system solves "
":math:`G^2 p^2 + (1 - \\beta) p - \\alpha = 0`, whose positive root is"
msgstr ""
"O **ponto fixo** do sistema combinado mapa‑mais‑filtro resolve :math:`G^2"
" p^2 + (1 - \\beta) p - \\alpha = 0`, cuja raiz positiva é"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:152
msgid ""
"p^{+} = \\frac{2\\alpha}{(1-\\beta) + \\sqrt{(1-\\beta)^2 + 4\\alpha "
"G^2}},"
msgstr ""
"p^{+} = \\frac{2\\alpha}{(1-\\beta) + \\sqrt{(1-\\beta)^2 + 4\\alpha "
"G^2}},"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:156
msgid ""
"with :math:`G = \\sum_k c_k` the DC gain.  This cancellation‑free form is"
" the one used by the code (it stays accurate as :math:`G \\to 0`).  For "
"the system to have a bounded attractor, the fixed point must be finite "
"and the filter must be stable (all poles inside the unit circle)."
msgstr ""
"com :math:`G = \\sum_k c_k` o ganho DC.  Esta forma sem cancelamento é a "
"usada pelo código (permanece precisa quando :math:`G \\to 0`).  Para que "
"o sistema tenha um atrator limitado, o ponto fixo deve ser finito e o "
"filtro deve ser estável (todos os polos dentro do círculo unitário)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:161
msgid ""
"The function :func:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.lyapunov_max` handles "
"the 4‑D pole‑filtered variant, which introduces an additional stability "
"parameter (pole radius :math:`r`) that must satisfy :math:`0 \\le r < 1`."
msgstr ""
"The function :func:`~chaotic_pfc.dynamics.lyapunov.lyapunov_max` handles "
"the 4‑D pole‑filtered variant, which introduces an additional stability "
"parameter (pole radius :math:`r`) that must satisfy :math:`0 \\\\le r < "
"1`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:166
msgid "Known limitations"
msgstr "Limitações conhecidas"

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:168
msgid ""
"**Cutoff extremes.**  :math:`\\omega_c \\to 0` produces a filter that "
"passes almost nothing (all‑stop); :math:`\\omega_c \\to 1` passes almost "
"everything (all‑pass).  Both extremes degenerate the filter and produce "
"behaviour indistinguishable from the unfiltered map — the sweep grid "
"excludes :math:`\\omega_c = 0` and :math:`\\omega_c = 1`."
msgstr ""
"**Extremos de corte.**  :math:`\\omega_c \\to 0` produz um filtro que "
"quase não passa nada (rejeita tudo); :math:`\\omega_c \\to 1` passa quase"
" tudo (passa-tudo).  Ambos os extremos degeneram o filtro e produzem "
"comportamento indistinguível do mapa sem filtro — a grade da varredura "
"exclui :math:`\\omega_c = 0` e :math:`\\omega_c = 1`."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:174
msgid ""
"**Order limits.**  For :math:`N_z \\ge 40`, the filter design becomes "
"numerically ill‑conditioned (the window function has extreme values at "
"the filter edges).  The sweep currently tops at :math:`N_z = 40` "
"(:math:`N_s = 41`)."
msgstr ""
"**Limites de ordem.**  Para :math:`N_z \\ge 40`, o projeto do filtro "
"torna-se numericamente mal-condicionado (a função de janela tem valores "
"extremos nas bordas do filtro).  A varredura vai atualmente até "
":math:`N_z = 40` (:math:`N_s = 41`)."

#: ../../source/algorithms/fir_design.rst:179
msgid ""
"**DC gain.**  FIR filters designed with ``firwin`` have a DC gain of "
"approximately 1.0 for lowpass , but not exactly, due to window tapering."
"  The chaotic map is sensitive to the exact coefficient magnitudes, which"
" is why the FIR bank is precomputed once rather than reconstructed per "
"grid point."
msgstr ""
"**Ganho DC.**  Filtros FIR projetados com ``firwin`` têm ganho DC de "
"aproximadamente 1,0 para passa-baixas, mas não exatamente, devido ao "
"janelamento.  O mapa caótico é sensível às magnitudes exatas dos "
"coeficientes, razão pela qual o banco FIR é pré-computado uma vez em vez "
"de reconstruído por ponto da grade."

